      "description": "Watch Sassuolo vs Frosinone highlights and goals from Coppa Italia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 2, 2026. The Coppa Italia delivered a night of high tension on September 2, 2026 , as Sassuolo and Frosinone locked horns in a knockout clash that tested the nerves of both sets of supporters. Both teams entered the pitch with high ambitions, resulting in a physical and tactical battle that remained undecided until the very last moments. First Half Resilience and Equalizer The match ignited in the 36th minute when Frosinone broke the deadlock. Benjamin Dominguez proved to be the difference-maker in the early stages, finding the net to give the visitors a crucial lead. Sassuolo , determined not to let the game slip away at home, ramped up the pressure as the first half drew to a close. Their persistence paid off in stoppage time. In the 45+2nd minute, Luis Hasa provided a pinpoint assist for Aleksa Terzic , who clinicaly finished the chance to level the score. The equalizer just before the interval shifted the momentum, leaving both managers with plenty to discuss during the break after an intense opening 45 minutes. Tactical Shifts and Defensive Discipline The second half was characterized by a series of tactical adjustments and rising temperatures on the field. Discipline became a factor as the referee issued yellow cards to Kevin Akpoguma , Simone Cinquegrano , and Stefano Turati . Substitutions followed as both sides searched for a winner; Domenico Berardi and Armand Lauriente were introduced for Sassuolo , while Frosinone brought on Tomas Bobcek to bolster their attack. Despite the fresh legs and late-game pressure, neither side could find the decisive goal in regulation time. As the final whistle blew with the score still locked at 1-1, the match headed into a dramatic penalty shootout to determine who would progress to the next round. Penalty Shootout Drama The shootout began with immediate heartbreak for the home side as Luis Hasa and Wisdom Amey missed their attempts. Although Kristian Thorstvedt , Sebastiano Esposito , and Domenico Berardi all converted their spot-kicks, the early misses put Sassuolo in a difficult position. Frosinone , conversely, showed remarkable composure from the spot. Darryl Bakola , Alessio Zerbin , Omar Fayed , and finally Tomas Bobcek all found the back of the net with clinical precision. Their flawless execution in the shootout secured Frosinone 's victory, marking a successful night in the Coppa Italia and sending them through to the next stage of the competition."
