      "description": "Watch Sassuolo vs Torino highlights and goals from Serie A on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 29, 2026. The match between Sassuolo and Torino promised a tactical showdown in the Serie A , with both sides looking to impose their style of play. On August 29, 2026, the pitch at the stadium hosted a fierce contest that demanded patience and precision from every player involved. First Half Breakthroughs After a cagey opening period, the deadlock was broken in the 32nd minute by Cristian Volpato . With a clever left-footed strike from outside the box, he managed to beat the keeper, giving Sassuolo the lead. The hosts could not rest on their laurels, however, as Torino pushed for an equalizer before the halftime whistle. Their efforts were rewarded in the 45+2 minute when Pietro Comuzzo headed home from an Alessio Cacciamani assist, leveling the score and ensuring the second half would be a test of nerves. Defining the Result The second half saw an increase in tactical substitutions as both managers sought to gain an edge through fresh legs. The physicality grew, with several yellow cards issued as the game reached its boiling point. The pivotal moment arrived in the 78th minute: Fedde Leysen delivered a crucial assist to Domenico Berardi , who calmly found the back of the net with his left foot. Despite late pressure from the visitors, Sassuolo maintained their composure to protect the narrow advantage until the final whistle signaled the end of a hard-fought encounter."
